1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:03,017
Your tests are green. But is your code safe?

2
00:00:03,567 --> 00:00:06,716
A test only checks what someone thought to test.

3
00:00:06,716 --> 00:00:08,159
A hard coded password,

4
00:00:08,159 --> 00:00:08,947
a weak hash,

5
00:00:08,947 --> 00:00:11,439
a bug in a rare branch: no test fails.

6
00:00:11,989 --> 00:00:13,697
SonarQube reads every line,

7
00:00:13,697 --> 00:00:14,856
without running it.

8
00:00:14,856 --> 00:00:16,502
It tells you what is wrong,

9
00:00:16,502 --> 00:00:16,868
where,

10
00:00:16,868 --> 00:00:17,600
and how bad.

11
00:00:18,150 --> 00:00:20,134
Today: what static analysis is,

12
00:00:20,134 --> 00:00:21,670
the words you must know,

13
00:00:21,670 --> 00:00:24,166
and a live tour of the real SonarQube.

14
00:00:25,716 --> 00:00:27,145
Here is what to expect.

15
00:00:27,695 --> 00:00:29,189
One: four words to know.

16
00:00:29,739 --> 00:00:33,344
Two: how SonarQube sorts every problem, in three groups.

17
00:00:33,894 --> 00:00:36,692
Three: a live tour of the real SonarQube,

18
00:00:36,692 --> 00:00:38,290
on real CloudCart code.

19
00:00:38,290 --> 00:00:38,890
Projects,

20
00:00:38,890 --> 00:00:39,689
the summary,

21
00:00:39,689 --> 00:00:40,422
the issues,

22
00:00:40,422 --> 00:00:41,554
the quality gate,

23
00:00:41,554 --> 00:00:43,153
and the quality profile.

24
00:00:43,703 --> 00:00:46,519
Four: the common mistakes, and where to find the lab.

25
00:00:47,069 --> 00:00:49,927
This is objective one of the SonarQube domain.

26
00:00:51,477 --> 00:00:52,693
Four words to know.

27
00:00:53,243 --> 00:00:56,251
Static analysis: reading the code, without running it.

28
00:00:56,801 --> 00:01:00,001
Issue: one problem, found by one rule, in one place.

29
00:01:00,551 --> 00:01:03,580
Quality profile: the set of rules that are switched on.

30
00:01:04,130 --> 00:01:07,352
Quality gate: a pass or fail decision, for the new code.

31
00:01:07,902 --> 00:01:13,512
Analysis, issue, profile, gate. Everything else in SonarQube is built from these four.

32
00:01:15,062 --> 00:01:17,985
Every issue belongs to one of three software qualities.

33
00:01:18,535 --> 00:01:23,164
Security: can someone abuse this? A hard coded password, or a weak hash.

34
00:01:23,714 --> 00:01:26,392
Reliability: can this break while it runs?

35
00:01:26,392 --> 00:01:26,774
A bug,

36
00:01:26,774 --> 00:01:28,050
like a null pointer,

37
00:01:28,050 --> 00:01:29,325
or a thread problem.

38
00:01:29,875 --> 00:01:32,473
Maintainability: is this hard to change?

39
00:01:32,473 --> 00:01:33,512
Duplicated code,

40
00:01:33,512 --> 00:01:35,656
or a method that is far too long.

41
00:01:36,206 --> 00:01:39,043
Each issue also has a severity: blocker,

42
00:01:39,043 --> 00:01:39,398
high,

43
00:01:39,398 --> 00:01:39,894
medium,

44
00:01:39,894 --> 00:01:40,178
low,

45
00:01:40,178 --> 00:01:40,745
or info.

46
00:01:40,745 --> 00:01:41,525
The rating,

47
00:01:41,525 --> 00:01:42,376
from A to E,

48
00:01:42,376 --> 00:01:44,291
comes from the worst issue.

49
00:01:44,841 --> 00:01:47,400
Then one big idea: clean as you code.

50
00:01:47,400 --> 00:01:49,060
Judge new code strictly,

51
00:01:49,060 --> 00:01:51,135
and fix old code step by step.

52
00:01:51,685 --> 00:01:54,010
That is why the quality gate looks at new code.

53
00:01:55,560 --> 00:01:56,806
A real SonarQube,

54
00:01:56,806 --> 00:01:57,914
Community Build,

55
00:01:57,914 --> 00:01:59,575
running on this machine.

56
00:01:59,575 --> 00:02:00,960
We sign in as admin.

57
00:02:00,960 --> 00:02:02,829
The first page is Projects.

58
00:02:02,829 --> 00:02:04,422
It lists every project,

59
00:02:04,422 --> 00:02:06,430
with its quality gate result,

60
00:02:06,430 --> 00:02:07,537
and its ratings.

61
00:02:07,537 --> 00:02:08,922
We have one project,

62
00:02:08,922 --> 00:02:09,683
CloudCart.

63
00:02:09,683 --> 00:02:10,237
Open it.

64
00:02:19,287 --> 00:02:21,021
This is the Summary page.

65
00:02:21,021 --> 00:02:21,783
At the top,

66
00:02:21,783 --> 00:02:23,517
the quality gate: Passed.

67
00:02:23,517 --> 00:02:24,141
Below it,

68
00:02:24,141 --> 00:02:25,458
two tabs: New Code,

69
00:02:25,458 --> 00:02:26,637
and Overall Code.

70
00:02:26,637 --> 00:02:28,786
We are looking at overall code,

71
00:02:28,786 --> 00:02:30,381
all nine hundred lines.

72
00:02:30,931 --> 00:02:32,359
Now the three tiles,

73
00:02:32,359 --> 00:02:34,430
the three software qualities.

74
00:02:34,430 --> 00:02:36,430
Security: three open issues,

75
00:02:36,430 --> 00:02:37,073
rating D.

76
00:02:37,073 --> 00:02:39,358
Reliability: eleven open issues,

77
00:02:39,358 --> 00:02:40,001
rating D.

78
00:02:40,001 --> 00:02:41,572
Maintainability: zero,

79
00:02:41,572 --> 00:02:42,215
rating A.

80
00:02:42,215 --> 00:02:42,858
Remember,

81
00:02:42,858 --> 00:02:45,000
the rating is the worst issue.

82
00:02:45,000 --> 00:02:47,357
One high issue is enough for a D.

83
00:02:47,907 --> 00:02:49,459
Further down: coverage,

84
00:02:49,459 --> 00:02:50,606
and duplications.

85
00:02:50,606 --> 00:02:52,292
Coverage is zero percent,

86
00:02:52,292 --> 00:02:54,653
because we sent no coverage report.

87
00:02:54,653 --> 00:02:56,137
Duplications are zero.

88
00:02:56,137 --> 00:03:00,792
Notice the warning: Community Build does not scan every kind of file.

89
00:03:00,792 --> 00:03:02,883
Know what your tool cannot see.

90
00:03:03,433 --> 00:03:04,674
Now the Issues page.

91
00:03:04,674 --> 00:03:05,418
On the left,

92
00:03:05,418 --> 00:03:06,163
the filters.

93
00:03:06,163 --> 00:03:06,969
On the right,

94
00:03:06,969 --> 00:03:08,582
the list: fourteen issues,

95
00:03:08,582 --> 00:03:11,497
and about four hours of effort to fix them all.

96
00:03:12,047 --> 00:03:13,878
Filter by software quality.

97
00:03:13,878 --> 00:03:14,962
Choose Security.

98
00:03:14,962 --> 00:03:17,402
Now only the security issues remain,

99
00:03:17,402 --> 00:03:20,453
and every item is a risk someone could abuse.

100
00:03:21,003 --> 00:03:22,266
Open the first one.

101
00:03:22,266 --> 00:03:23,729
A weak hash algorithm,

102
00:03:23,729 --> 00:03:24,926
in LegacyPricing.

103
00:03:24,926 --> 00:03:25,857
The first tab,

104
00:03:25,857 --> 00:03:27,120
Where is the issue,

105
00:03:27,120 --> 00:03:28,450
shows the real code,

106
00:03:28,450 --> 00:03:29,048
the line,

107
00:03:29,048 --> 00:03:30,112
and the message.

108
00:03:30,662 --> 00:03:35,633
The second tab: Why is this an issue. The rule explains the risk, in plain words.

109
00:03:36,183 --> 00:03:38,156
The third tab: How can I fix it.

110
00:03:38,156 --> 00:03:39,452
It shows a safer way,

111
00:03:39,452 --> 00:03:40,438
with an example.

112
00:03:40,438 --> 00:03:42,412
You never have to guess the fix.

113
00:03:42,962 --> 00:03:44,378
Now the quality gate.

114
00:03:44,378 --> 00:03:45,322
Open Policies,

115
00:03:45,322 --> 00:03:46,604
then Quality gates.

116
00:03:46,604 --> 00:03:48,357
This is the built in gate,

117
00:03:48,357 --> 00:03:49,503
called Sonar way.

118
00:03:49,503 --> 00:03:52,808
Its conditions are about new code: no new issues,

119
00:03:52,808 --> 00:03:54,022
hotspots reviewed,

120
00:03:54,022 --> 00:03:56,450
coverage of at least eighty percent,

121
00:03:56,450 --> 00:03:59,282
and duplications of at most three percent.

122
00:03:59,832 --> 00:04:01,282
And quality profiles.

123
00:04:01,282 --> 00:04:04,251
A profile is the list of rules switched on,

124
00:04:04,251 --> 00:04:05,494
for each language.

125
00:04:05,494 --> 00:04:07,704
Java uses the profile Sonar way.

126
00:04:08,254 --> 00:04:09,394
That is the tour.

127
00:04:09,394 --> 00:04:09,930
Project,

128
00:04:09,930 --> 00:04:10,399
issues,

129
00:04:10,399 --> 00:04:10,801
rules,

130
00:04:10,801 --> 00:04:11,136
gate,

131
00:04:11,136 --> 00:04:11,941
and profile.

132
00:04:11,941 --> 00:04:13,684
Back on the Projects page,

133
00:04:13,684 --> 00:04:15,091
the gate says Passed,

134
00:04:15,091 --> 00:04:17,370
because it only looks at new code.

135
00:04:17,370 --> 00:04:18,711
In the next lessons,

136
00:04:18,711 --> 00:04:19,985
we install our own,

137
00:04:19,985 --> 00:04:21,459
and scan our own code.

138
00:04:23,009 --> 00:04:24,161
Five mistakes.

139
00:04:24,711 --> 00:04:28,480
One: treating a green quality gate as proof that the code is good.

140
00:04:28,480 --> 00:04:30,194
The gate only checks new code.

141
00:04:30,744 --> 00:04:36,013
Two: trying to fix every old issue in one week. Fix new code first. Clean as you code.

142
00:04:36,563 --> 00:04:40,851
Three: ignoring the rating. One high issue makes the whole rating a D.

143
00:04:41,401 --> 00:04:46,265
Four: thinking the tool sees everything. Read the warnings about files it cannot scan.

144
00:04:46,815 --> 00:04:52,255
Five: switching off a rule, because it is noisy. Ask why it fires, before you silence it.

145
00:04:53,805 --> 00:04:56,600
Where to find the lab. Pause here, and write it down.

146
00:04:57,150 --> 00:04:58,614
One: the repository,

147
00:04:58,614 --> 00:05:02,934
github.com/it-waves/devops-ai,

148
00:05:02,934 --> 00:05:05,278
in the folder academy slash lab.

149
00:05:05,828 --> 00:05:11,801
Two: the files, lab164.sh, and shortcuts164.sh.

150
00:05:12,351 --> 00:05:17,812
Three: install it, with sudo install, into /usr/local/sbin.

151
00:05:18,362 --> 00:05:24,250
Four: load the short names, with source shortcuts164.sh. Then lab files.

152
00:05:24,800 --> 00:05:29,792
Five: lab files writes the demo file with seeded defects into your CloudCart.

153
00:05:29,792 --> 00:05:31,072
Lab down removes it.

154
00:05:31,622 --> 00:05:34,822
Six: you install your own SonarQube in the next lesson.

155
00:05:35,372 --> 00:05:37,015
The link is in the description.

156
00:05:38,565 --> 00:05:39,440
Your turn.

157
00:05:39,990 --> 00:05:43,851
One: write down the four words, and say each one in your own sentence.

158
00:05:44,401 --> 00:05:48,220
Two: name the three software qualities, with one example of each.

159
00:05:48,770 --> 00:05:52,396
Three: explain, in one sentence, what clean as you code means.

160
00:05:52,946 --> 00:05:54,055
Four: if you can,

161
00:05:54,055 --> 00:05:55,359
open any SonarQube,

162
00:05:55,359 --> 00:05:58,749
and find the Issues page and the Quality gates page.

163
00:05:59,299 --> 00:06:03,182
Five: tell a friend why a green test run does not mean safe code.

164
00:06:03,732 --> 00:06:05,460
Pause the video, and do it now.

165
00:06:21,010 --> 00:06:21,885
Quick check.

166
00:06:22,435 --> 00:06:24,141
What does static analysis mean?

167
00:06:24,691 --> 00:06:26,611
Name the three software qualities.

168
00:06:27,161 --> 00:06:28,868
What does a quality gate decide?

169
00:06:29,418 --> 00:06:31,082
What does clean as you code mean?

170
00:06:31,632 --> 00:06:33,964
Objective covered: MC18,

171
00:06:33,964 --> 00:06:34,984
objective one.

172
00:06:34,984 --> 00:06:36,150
Static analysis,

173
00:06:36,150 --> 00:06:37,170
quality gates,

174
00:06:37,170 --> 00:06:37,826
profiles,

175
00:06:37,826 --> 00:06:38,992
and issue types.

176
00:06:39,542 --> 00:06:41,611
Pause the video, and answer out loud.

177
00:06:52,161 --> 00:06:55,297
